{
  "$note": [
    "Written by hand from the Literals table (docs/reference/port-types.md, Literals); never generated.",
    "A row grades one literal against one declared type. `value` absent or null is a null literal; `accepted` is the verdict. A `note` says why a row is there.",
    "An accepted DateTime row with `instant` states the value the C# reader makes of it, as the text it is written as: text with no offset is UTC, and text with an offset or Z keeps it. The TypeScript half grades a DateTime as a JSON string and reads no instant.",
    "A row with `text` in place of `value` spells the literal as raw JSON text; `duplicateMember` marks text that repeats a member name, which the stored-document reader refuses (stored-document rule L3, docs/reference/validation-findings.md) and a parsed TypeScript value cannot hold.",
    "Read by both halves: C# PortLiteralVectorTests and TypePhaseTests, TypeScript literalCoercion.test.ts.",
    "`hostAtoms` and `hostConstructors` are the records the host types are registered with (a null `literal` or a null atom is a record with no form); a type they do not list is not registered."
  ],
